> Scope and provenance

Source partitions, fitting-only transformations, explicit update/generation loops and independent deployment guards are retained. Native preparation manifests record the recovered source hashes and protocol. The small models and samples are teaching experiments; no full-paper reproduction, benchmark ranking or unrecorded external parity is claimed.

> Held-out sentiment confusion matrix

Counts come from the original deployed predictions ledger, with rows as truth and columns as predictions. Sequence ledgers exclude padding; token accuracy and entity-span F1 answer different questions. Class IDs retain the original preparation ontology recorded in the manifest.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/imdb_lstm_sentiment_confusion.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::ifstream in("build/recovered-language/models/imdb_lstm/predictions.tsv");if(!in)throw std::runtime_error("actual held-out predictions missing");std::string header;std::getline(in,header);dm::nn::ConfusionMatrix matrix(2);size_t count=0;int id,length,truth,prediction,baseline;while(in>>id>>length>>truth>>prediction>>baseline){matrix.add(truth,prediction);++count;}if(!count)throw std::runtime_error("empty held-out predictions");std::print("Counted {} held-out sentiment decisions; padded positions excluded by the source ledger.\n",count);dm::nn::ConfusionMatrixPlotOptions options;options.title="imdb lstm actual held-out sentiment";matrix.save_svg("build/imdb_lstm_sentiment_confusion.svg",options);}
